====================================================================
PolyKernel T36 Wave 7: NEGATIVE evidence - blocked task does NOT fire
  A task that is @activate-d but left @block-ed must NOT fire (no
  premature fire) until @unblock releases it - even when its input
  wavelet has already arrived. The rendezvous rule "a task runs only
  when activated AND unblocked" gates firing.
  Also negative: a compute task (data task bound to TWO input colors)
  does NOT fire after only ONE input arrives - it waits for BOTH.
  (GPU-free functional simulator; no Cerebras hardware involved.)
====================================================================

### [1] standalone scheduler_test, blocked-task negative ###

Running main() from /build/source/googletest/src/gtest_main.cc
Note: Google Test filter = scheduler.BlockedTaskDoesNotFireUntilUnblocked:scheduler.ControlTaskGatedByRendezvous
